# TaskSignal UI And UX Polish Rules

TaskSignal is a product-register interface. Design serves the workflow. The target feeling is dense, calm, transparent, trustworthy, technical, utilitarian, and research-grade.

## Preserve The Design System

- Use the existing restrained product system: cool tinted background, tinted white surfaces, deep ink text, cool slate muted text, restrained teal primary action and selection, amber for scoring or attention states, cool slate hairline borders.
- Keep the system font stack and fixed product type scale. Do not introduce display fonts.
- Prefer tokens and shared utilities over hard-coded one-off values.
- Cards are only for bounded summaries, repeated evidence items, and focused panels. Do not nest cards.
- Keep the desktop left navigation and single-column mobile flow.
- Use lucide-react icons already present in the project.

## Hallmark Guardrails

- No invented metrics, fake proof bars, testimonials, logos, adoption numbers, or review claims.
- No gradient text.
- No decorative glassmorphism.
- No fake browser chrome, fake IDE chrome, fake phone frames, or fake terminal windows.
- No colored side-stripe borders wider than 1px on cards, list items, callouts, alerts, or blockquotes.
- No identical icon plus heading plus paragraph card grids as the dominant structure.
- No generic hero-first marketing page when the useful product workflow should be visible.
- Preserve route ownership and component boundaries. Do not delete route trees or production components unless the user approved a file-level deletion plan.

## Impeccable Product Polish

- Align first, then polish. Name drift as missing token, one-off implementation, or conceptual misalignment.
- Every interactive element needs default, hover, focus-visible, active, disabled, loading, error where relevant, and success where relevant.
- Focus indicators must remain visible and high contrast.
- Loading states should be skeletons or clear inline state, not only centered spinners.
- Empty states should teach the next action.
- Error states need recovery paths and should preserve audit context.
- Motion must convey state only, 150 to 250 ms, no bounce or elastic, and respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Use predictable product patterns: side nav, page headers, tables, filters, tabs or segmented controls when useful, inline actions where possible.

## TaskSignal-Specific UX Priorities

- Make the main journey obvious: process fixture data, review ranked opportunities, inspect evidence, export a Codex-ready prompt.
- Keep fixture mode and live scans visually distinct. Fixture mode should feel safe and reproducible; live scans should expose source, query, limit, status, and errors.
- Put evidence and score rationale ahead of decoration.
- Make source attribution visible near evidence.
- Show privacy posture where it matters: public sources, source URLs, author hashes, no raw usernames.
- Tables should scan quickly on desktop and degrade responsibly on mobile.
- Long opportunity titles, queries, URLs, and prompt content must wrap without breaking layout.

## Responsive And Accessibility Floor

Verify at 320, 375, 414, 768, 1024, and desktop widths.

- No horizontal page scroll. Tables may scroll inside their own region.
- Touch targets should be at least 44 px on touch layouts.
- Text must not overflow buttons, badges, nav items, cards, panels, or fixed-width columns.
- Use semantic headings, labels, buttons, links, table headers, and status messaging.
- Preserve keyboard navigation and logical tab order.

## Preferred Files To Improve

- `apps/web/src/components/ui.tsx`: shared primitives and states.
- `apps/web/src/components/app-shell.tsx`: active nav, mobile nav, skip link, shell density.
- `apps/web/src/app/globals.css`: tokens, focus, reduced motion, background restraint.
- `apps/web/src/features/dashboard.tsx`: workflow hierarchy, live scan controls, metrics, table, chart empty states.
- `apps/web/src/features/opportunity-detail.tsx`: score explanation, evidence hierarchy, attribution, prompt/export actions.
- `apps/web/src/features/prompt-view.tsx`: prompt copy/download workflow, loading/error/success states.
- `apps/web/src/features/scans.tsx`, `sources.tsx`, `search.tsx`: consistency, empty/loading/error states, scanability.
